From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] A local light in a shadow

Patch 0022 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

A fairy's glow does not lift the bridge's shadow where it lies on the water. That is the same
complaint that began this work on 2026-09-28, on a different surface, and it is worth being clear
that the arithmetic behind it is not a bug.

The factor this pass writes is the light that REACHES a surface over the light the game already
gave it, and the denominator is the UNSHADOWED full light. In a sunlit scene that denominator
carries the whole sun, so a local light worth a fraction of the sun moves the ratio very little,
and the knee above the game's own full light then compresses whatever it does add. A light in
shade is therefore quiet by construction, which is right for a candle and wrong for the thing the
user keeps describing as a torch in a tunnel.

Two parts of that can be loosened and they are different, so they are separate rungs rather than
one tuning:

  31  the local light is added AFTER the knee, so it is never compressed
  32  the local light counts for more where the sun is BLOCKED, in proportion to how much of the
      sun is missing at that surface: nothing in full sun, double in full shadow
  33  both

Offered as rungs because the user's standing instruction for this area is "dont guess, add rungs
to test", and because which of these looks right is a judgment about the game's look rather than
something the code can settle.

With the ray tracing row Off none of this runs.
---
diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -994,9 +994,38 @@ void DirectRayGen() {
     // light in the shade adds every bit of itself); the EXCESS above it is compressed, one over
     // one plus itself, so a strong light on a sunlit wall reads as a glow and never as white.
     // The same knee holds the bounce and the sun's own overshoot.
-    const float3 shadedRaw = bounceTerm + sunTermShaded + local;
+    // A LOCAL LIGHT IN A SHADOW (rungs 31 to 33, the user 2026-09-30: a fairy's glow does not
+    // lift the bridge's shadow where it lies on the water, which is the same complaint that
+    // began this work on 2026-09-28 on a different surface).
+    //
+    // The arithmetic is why, and it is not a bug: the factor is the light that REACHES a surface
+    // over the light the game already gave it, and `lit` is the UNSHADOWED full light. In a
+    // sunlit scene that denominator carries the whole sun, so a fairy worth a fraction of the sun
+    // moves the ratio very little, and the knee then compresses whatever she adds above `lit`.
+    // Two things can be loosened and they are different, so they are separate rungs.
+    //
+    //   31  her light is added AFTER the knee, so it is never compressed
+    //   32  her light counts for more where the sun is BLOCKED, in proportion to how much of the
+    //       sun is missing, which is what makes a torch read as a torch in a tunnel
+    //   33  both
+    const float rung = RtParams.tuneExperiment.x;
+    const bool localAfterKnee = (rung == 31.0f) || (rung == 33.0f);
+    const bool localLiftsShade = (rung == 32.0f) || (rung == 33.0f);
+    float3 localTerm = local;
+    if (localLiftsShade) {
+        // How much of the sun this surface is missing, per channel, as a share of the sun it
+        // would have had. Nothing in full sun, everything in full shadow.
+        const float3 sunFull = max(sunColor * ndl, 0.0f);
+        const float3 missing = max(sunFull - sunTermShaded, 0.0f);
+        const float3 share = saturate(missing / max(sunFull, 1.0e-4f));
+        localTerm = local * (1.0f + share);
+    }
+    const float3 shadedRaw = bounceTerm + sunTermShaded + (localAfterKnee ? float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f) : localTerm);
     const float3 excess = max(shadedRaw - lit, 0.0f);
-    const float3 shaded = min(min(shadedRaw, lit) + excess / (1.0f + excess), shadeCap);
+    float3 shaded = min(min(shadedRaw, lit) + excess / (1.0f + excess), shadeCap);
+    if (localAfterKnee) {
+        shaded = min(shaded + localTerm, shadeCap);
+    }
     float3 factor;
     factor.x = (lit.x > 1.0e-4f) ? (shaded.x / lit.x) : 1.0f;
     factor.y = (lit.y > 1.0e-4f) ? (shaded.y / lit.y) : 1.0f;
